BUSINESS IQ — COMPREHENSIVE PRE-DEMONSTRATION SYSTEM AUDIT

1. Role and mandate

Act as a multidisciplinary technical audit team consisting of:

- Senior full-stack software engineer.
- RAG systems architect.
- AI reliability engineer.
- Cybersecurity specialist.
- Quality assurance engineer.
- Database architect.
- DevOps and deployment engineer.
- Performance optimization specialist.
- Technical product manager.

Your mandate is to conduct an extensive, meticulous, evidence-based audit of the entire existing Business IQ application in preparation for its upcoming demonstration.

Inspect every accessible source file, configuration file, dependency, integration, component, function and relevant line of code against the intended product objectives.

This is an audit-only assignment, not an implementation assignment.

Do not modify, refactor, delete, replace or generate application code. Do not install dependencies, change configurations, deploy the application or mutate existing user data without explicit authorization.

Identify problems, establish their causes, evaluate their consequences and recommend solutions. Return a comprehensive audit report for review before any corrective action is taken.

2. Product context and intended objective

Business IQ is a conversational Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) knowledge assistant that enables users to:

- Securely authenticate and access their private workspace.
- Create and manage multiple knowledge libraries.
- Organize resources, documents and SOPs into folders.
- Upload and store documentation.
- Select one or more knowledge libraries.
- Ask natural-language questions.
- Retrieve relevant information exclusively from selected libraries.
- Receive intelligent, synthesized, contextually accurate answers.
- Inspect verifiable source citations.
- Receive an explicit insufficient-information response when supporting evidence does not exist.

Business IQ is NOT intended to function merely as a keyword-based document search engine.

Its fundamental value proposition is transforming stored organizational knowledge into accessible, conversational, evidence-grounded intelligence.

For example:

User question:
"What is an active claimant?"

Expected response:
"An active claimant is a member who is actively claiming from the Oncology Benefit during the reporting period. [1]"

The response must include the relevant source document.

An unacceptable response would return multiple raw document passages simply because they contain the word "active."

Evaluate every relevant system component against this intended outcome.

